sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant T as eSSL or ZKTeco Terminal, illustrative serial T-PUNE-01
    participant R as Tenant-scoped Push Receiver URL+secret
    participant A as Auth and Device Registry
    participant M as device_user to employee_id map
    participant S as Punch Store dedup + tamper-evident
    participant E as Attendance Engine FR-ATT-001 ledger

    Note over T,R: No middleware / no static IP / no port-forward - device HTTP-POSTs outbound
    T->>R: Handshake with serial and secret or token
    R->>A: Authenticate serial to this tenant
    alt Serial unknown or wrong tenant
        A-->>R: Reject
        R-->>T: Rejected and logged - multi-tenant isolation, AC3
    else Authorized
        A-->>R: OK, tenant-scoped
    end
    loop Heartbeat - last-seen and clock skew, FR-DEV-003
        T->>R: Heartbeat with device-local clock
        R->>R: Measure offset vs NTP-synced server time, alert if unseen over threshold before lock
    end

    Note over T,R: Long-weekend outage Fri 18:00 to Mon 09:00 - 42 workers punch to local store
    T->>R: POST attendance-log batch - about 168 buffered records, late, out of order, some Fri retries
    R->>S: Persist raw punches with payload_hash and device-local, UTC and tz times
    S->>S: De-dup on sn, user, ts, direction plus payload_hash - AC4
    S->>S: Check verify mode against consent - biometric without consent raises exception, punch kept, erasure queued, FR-DEV-008 AC3
    R-->>T: ACK batch - device marks delivered, stops re-flooding, AC2
    T->>R: Command poll
    R-->>T: Queued commands incl. delete-template for erased employees, or empty
    T->>R: Command acknowledgement - closes the per-device erasure item, FR-DEV-007

    S->>M: Resolve device_user_id to employee_id, effective-dated
    alt Device user unmapped
        M-->>S: Enrollment exception - punch retained, backfilled on mapping, FR-DEV-002 AC1
    else Mapped
        M-->>S: employee_id
    end
    S->>E: Emit events attributed to Fri, Sat, Sun pay dates - capture time, not sync time
    E->>E: Recompute affected past dates plus weekend OT and substituted-rest-day lines - AC5
    alt Prior period already locked
        E->>E: Open retro run against the period rule version - FR-ATT-001 AC3
    else Open period
        E->>E: Re-project day-status from the event log
    end
